# Template for `deployment/docker/.env.production-workers` (gitignored).
#
# Copy to `.env.production-workers` and fill in real values:
#
#     cp deployment/docker/.env.production-workers.example \
#        deployment/docker/.env.production-workers
#
# WHAT THIS IS
# ------------
# Environment overrides for the PRODUCTION converter worker replicas — the
# compose service `worker`, which runs as `docker-worker-1/2/3`. Compose loads
# the root `.env` first and this file second; later entries win, so anything set
# here overrides the development value.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS
# -------------
# Development and production intentionally share one Redis instance and one
# object bucket. That sharing leaks at the queue: a single consumer group
# competes for every message on a stream, so without isolation a job created in
# one environment is executed by a worker bound to the other environment's
# database. The damage is silent —
#
#   * `update_conversion_job` is a bare `UPDATE ... WHERE job_id = ?`. Against a
#     database that lacks the row it affects zero rows and raises nothing, so
#     the worker still ACKs the message and logs success while the owning
#     database's row stays `PENDING` forever, and
#   * `consume(user_id, ...)` would create or charge a credit bucket for that
#     numeric `user_id` in the wrong database, where the same id is almost
#     certainly a different person.
#
# Setting `QUEUE_STREAM_PREFIX` (empty here, `dev:` in `.env`) puts the two sets
# of workers on disjoint sets of stream keys, so neither can steal the other's
# jobs.
#
# PRODUCTION ITSELF NEEDS NOTHING
# -------------------------------
# The default prefix is the empty string, which reproduces the original stream
# names exactly. The deployed Render API and its configuration are unaffected by
# this feature; do not set `QUEUE_STREAM_PREFIX` there.

# Production database — NOT the `DATABASE_URL` in the root .env.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/neondb?ssl=require

# Empty on purpose: consume the real, unprefixed production stream names.
QUEUE_STREAM_PREFIX=
